FB_Task declaration:
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task
VAR_INPUT
 PartPulse : BOOL;
 Reset : BOOL;
 Target : USINT;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
 Count : USINT;
 Complete : BOOL;
 Error : BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR
 previous_pulse : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR

Implementation:

Error := (Target < 1) OR (Target > 20);
IF Error THEN
 Count := 0;
 Complete := FALSE;
ELSIF Reset THEN
 Count := 0;
 Complete := FALSE;
ELSE
 IF PartPulse AND NOT previous_pulse THEN
   IF Count < Target THEN
     Count := Count + 1;
   ELSE
     Count := Target; // saturation; but if shrink target, Count should clamp even no edge. Requirement "Shrinking Target clamps Count via min(..., Target) and re-evaluates Complete."
   END_IF
 END_IF
 // clamp regardless
 IF Count > Target THEN Count := Target; END_IF
 Complete := (Count >= Target);
END_IF
previous_pulse := PartPulse;

Need subtle: else !reset !invalid: countAfterEdge = min(qCount + (rise?1:0), Target). So Count := MIN(Count + BOOL_TO_USINT(rise), Target). Could write IF Count < Target AND rise THEN Count := Count+1; ELSIF Count > Target THEN Count := Target; END_IF. If Count == target no change. Good. In CODESYS MIN with USINT maybe generic. Simpler conditional:

IF PartPulse AND NOT previous_pulse AND (Count < Target) THEN
 Count := Count + 1;
ELSIF Count > Target THEN
 Count := Target;
END_IF;
Complete := Count >= Target;

If rise and Count > target (possible only target shrink from prior scan; but target available sampled this scan; target shrink). Then clamp target. If Count = Target and rise, no increment. Saturation good. If Count<Target and no rise count unchanged.

Edge memory updates every scan including reset/invalid. Yes assignment at end. Reset and invalid handled. Target type USINT valid domain 1..20. Target < 1 catches 0. Target >20.

Potential issue output initialization Count etc CODESYS defaults zero/false. Requirement exact initial. Could set in VAR_OUTPUT initializers? Count : USINT := 0 etc. But FB outputs retain. Initial instance values. We should initialize. previous_pulse := FALSE. Could do declaration initialization. Might be needed formal init. But output VAR initial may be supported. Use:
Count : USINT := 0;
Complete : BOOL := FALSE;
Error : BOOL := FALSE;
VAR previous_pulse : BOOL := FALSE; END_VAR
Likely fine.

Need perhaps DUT? No supporting objects [].

